entries.def:
ὑπερήφανος, -ον
(ὑπέρ, φαίνομαι, with η pleonast., see Kühner3, I, 189) [in LXX for זֵד, גֵּאֶה, לוּץ, etc. ;] 
showing oneself above others; 
__(a) in good sense (Plat., al.), pre-eminent, splendid; 
__(b) more frequently in had sense, and so always in Scr., arrogant, haughty, disdainful (see Westc. Epp. Jo., 65b): Rom.1.30, 2Ti.3.2; διανοίᾳ καρδίας, Luk.1.51 opposite to ταπεινός (as in Pro.3.34), Jas.4.6, 1Pe.5.5"…
